WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
At a Catholic baptism, water is
poured over a baby's head three times.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.950
Then oil called chrism
is traced on the head.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.810
A white garment goes on.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.480
A candle is lit.

5
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.550
To an outsider, it is just
water, oil and a flame.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.530
But Catholics count seven
sacraments like this,

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.520
from birth to death.

8
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.900
So how can ordinary things carry grace?

9
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:29.350
In this mission, you'll see the seven
sacraments sorted into three groups.

10
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.250
Then you'll follow a
baptism and a confirmation,

11
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.840
step by step, and see
what each sign means.

12
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:41.640
Your mission: explain how Catholics believe
ordinary things can carry God's grace.
